# Steep demo conventions

When the user asks for Steep metrics, Steep-as-code YAML, semantic modules, join
paths, KPIs, or "add metrics for [team]":

0. Read `agent-guidance.md` first. It is the source of truth for this repo and
   the client-facing handoff file.
1. Read `business-context.md`. Respect the sensitive-field deny list when
   choosing dimensions, and use team sections for `category` and `owner_emails`.
2. Follow `.cursor/skills/generate-steep-modules/SKILL.md` end-to-end when the
   skill is available.
3. Use `star-schema/models/marts/schema.yml` for module identifiers, physical
   schema and table names, default time columns, join hints, reference metrics,
   `example_values`, and dimension metadata.
4. Write output under `modules/`, one YAML file per module identifier, with
   two-space indentation and unique metric identifiers across all generated
   files.
5. Validate generated YAML before finishing. If local references and Steep's
   official product docs disagree, follow Steep.

If the user explicitly wants the portable client instructions, point them to
`agent-guidance.md`.
